WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.416
Raj: Each idempotent retry keeps its job key. Attempt identifiers remain separate for auditing.

2
00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:14.352
Priya: Okay, queued builds need state checks. Just to confirm, duplicates won't deploy?

3
00:00:14.352 --> 00:00:21.504
Lukas: Deployment uses its own idempotency ledger. Unknown outcomes stay held for reconciliation.

4
00:00:21.504 --> 00:00:28.632
Anika: Completed jobs won't rebuild unnecessarily, right? We can reuse their verified digest.

5
00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:37.056
Hannah: Only if build provenance still matches. Check signature, retention, and approval separately.

6
00:00:37.056 --> 00:00:44.280
Raj: The twelve failures have no deployment effects. Duplicate requests resolve to original jobs.

7
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:52.032
Lukas: Use bounded retries with backoff now. Authentication failures need repair, not repeated attempts.

8
00:00:52.032 --> 00:00:57.696
Priya: So, let the queue catch up slowly. Keep an eye on mirror latency.

9
00:00:57.696 --> 00:01:05.328
Hannah: Partial uploads have been quarantined too. A retry mustn't promote an incomplete object.

10
00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:12.240
Anika: Fair, I'll report pending work accurately. Held jobs aren't failures we can ignore.

